Usually, in a corridor (which is generally unlit) you only have sight range 
of the squares immediately adjacent to you.  So your pet is probably two 
squares (or more) away, and catches up while you're waiting.

There is only one way (that I can think of) where you on the same square as 
your pet, and that involves a saddle and an extended command (#ride)

If you are concerned about having your pet nearby, you can use a leash to 
keep them within a couple squares (but it's a bit of a hassle) or you can 
get yourself a magic whistle, which (while uncommon) is the ideal pet 
keeping item

